# Aberration

> Aberration is a continuous anomaly-detection platform for connected systems. It ingests MQTT sensor telemetry, runs streaming detection pipelines, calibrates anomaly scores with conformal methods and accumulates evidence until a change is flagged. Results are reviewable in a web dashboard and through an HTTP API.

One installation serves one organization. The dashboard and its API live at {{ frontend_base_url }}; the API is mounted under `/api`, so an OpenAPI path such as `/v1/anomalies` is called as `{{ frontend_base_url }}/api/v1/anomalies` with an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header from `POST /api/v1/auth/login`. Accounts are invitation-only.
{% if demo_base_url | default('') %}

A public, read-only demo at {{ demo_base_url }} streams open traffic data from Helsinki. Its listed read endpoints answer without a token, which makes it the place to try the API: for example `GET {{ demo_base_url }}/api/v1/monitors` or `GET {{ demo_base_url }}/api/v1/anomalies`. Writes answer 403.
{% endif %}

